b:
One thing no one has mentioned but I want to bring attention to: I think the forms are better balanced in Forsaken and shapeshifting is less of a hassle in Forsaken than in Apocalypse. In Apocalypse you roll Stamina + Primal Urge to shapeshift, each form has a different difficulty and the number of successes is based off how far the form you wish to shift to is from your current form. Shifting from Homid to Lupus is therefore the most difficult roll, requiring 4 successes. Don't have a dice pool of 4? Then you'll have to gradually shift forms until you're in the one you want. Or spend Rage and hope you don't frenzy. Also Primal Urge is a skill and it's skill you need to do the most basic werewolf thing imaginable, which means it's a skill everyone needs to spend dots on. Every single WoD game has something like this, some skill or background or ability that pretty much everyone needs. That's bad game design especially in an RPG.

&amp;#x200B;

In Forsaken you just shift as an immediate action into whichever form you desire. The only resource you need to spend is Essence and that just makes it go faster. Unless you're at Harmony five at which point shifting is a reflexive action, no Essence required. But wait it gets better: each form has its own associated free ability. This makes every form useful. Let me ask you something about Apocalypse: why would you ever use Hispo when the stat array for Crinos is so much better? The stats are better, the damage is better, and you can still wield weapons and klaives in Crinos. And since the majority of Apocalypse characters are going to be Homid breed, that only compounds the problem because Hispo is a harder form to take (Difficulty 7, 3 successes) than Crinos (Difficulty 6, 2 successes). There's literally no reason to ever take Hispo, it doesn't even cause Delirium. Why does that form even exist? In Forsaken the stats for Urshul are better balanced, a +2 to all physical abilities plus the ability to inflict combat tilts when you do damage. That's because Urshul is the default combat form, Gauru is the killing form, meant only when the chips are down and you need to make sure that every bastard in the room needs to die and die NOW!

&amp;#x200B;

TL;DR shapeshifting in Forsaken requires no rolls, brings no possibility of raging when you were just trying to sneak around as a wolf, and every form is useful and the stats for each form are better balanced.  


EDIT: I completely forgot about wolf senses. Forsaken is so much better about conveying and using the massive olfactory abilities of wolves than Apocalypse does. Tell me how often in Apocalypse did you use Lupus to go around sniffing for clues? Because in Forsaken there are many times where I've investigated a scene in Urhan going around sniffing at tables and the carpet.

